WEBVTT

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.680
<i>Soul Fist! Shadow Blade!</i>

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.850
<i>I'm totally sucking at this.</i>

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.420
<i>It's been way too long.</i>

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.720
<i>I haven't played one-on-one for a while.</i>

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.190
<i>Damn!</i>

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.410
<i>It feels like
I haven't defeated anyone lately.</i>

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.780
<i>My mind's in a haze.</i>

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.450
ORIGINAL WORK BY RENSUKE OSHIKIRI

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.410
<i>Haruo! You home?</i>

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.650
When do you want dinner?

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.550
I'm not really hungry.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.680
That's unusual.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.750
I wonder if that scooter made him carsick.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.290
<i>Jeez, I'm depressed.</i>

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.290
<i>I've lost my touch in fighting games.</i>

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.590
<i>When you were hitting with a Hane Yaiba,</i>

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:49.100
<i>your Kien Zan didn't come out
after your Kaeshi Yaiba.</i>

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.800
<i>That's right!</i>

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.330
<i>No, that's not the real problem.</i>

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.340
<i>I've got a pretty good idea
what the real cause is.</i>

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:04.010
<i>How can she look so forlorn like that?</i>

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.650
<i>That look, she seemed so tormented.</i>

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.850
<i>I never know what she's thinking,</i>

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.320
<i>but I think I understood this.</i>

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.490
<i>That we'll never again...</i>

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.290
<i>be as close as we used to.</i>

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.730
<i>I don't know when she made up her mind.</i>

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.670
<i>But judging from that look,
something must have happened.</i>

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.510
<i>The last time we met was when
we played games all night at her place.</i>

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.540
<i>Did something happen then?</i>

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.580
<i>It's all so unclear.</i>

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.950
<i>And why the heck am I so depressed?</i>

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:45.050
<i>Haruo, women are a mystery.</i>

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.520
<i>Certainly, you understand that by now.</i>

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:49.490
<i>You're suffering, right?</i>

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.330
<i>You can't make a move, right?</i>

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.360
<i>Why do you think that is?</i>

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.630
<i>Why do you think that is, Haruo?</i>

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.530
<i>What's causing your suffering?</i>

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.270
<i>Figure it out!</i>

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.510
<i>When I think about it,</i>

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.480
<i>she made me angry and got me really upset.</i>

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.190
<i>Just remembering those things,
I get really ticked off.</i>

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:22.660
<i>When did it start?</i>

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:28.200
<i>When did she become
such an important presence in my life?</i>

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.930
<i>Since sixth grade,</i>

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.670
<i>I've been on fire to battle her.</i>

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:35.870
<i>Is that all?</i>

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.610
<i>Were you only on fire to battle her?</i>

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.780
<i>Everywhere I go in town,</i>

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.920
<i>memories of our time together
come flooding back.</i>

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.260
<i>Wasn't it fun?</i>

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.460
<i>You must have had fun together.</i>

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.160
<i>Yes, it was fun.</i>

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.300
<i>Being with Ono was the best.</i>

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.100
<i>Weren't you on fire?</i>

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.970
<i>Wasn't your heart on fire too?</i>

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:09.940
<i>Yes, it was on fire.</i>

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.680
<i>Something other than
my desire to battle was on fire.</i>

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.810
<i>What was really on fire in your heart?</i>

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.950
<i>Face your heart, Haruo.</i>

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:28.690
<i>Honestly examine your heart and...</i>

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:29.820
<i>figure it out!</i>

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.100
I can't believe
you've come to my house, Haruo.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:43.940
My game console is finally
getting some use.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.010
It's ancient, though.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.610
And all you've got is dodge ball.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.180
I bought it so I could play with you.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.220
You know, you suck at this.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.820
That's because you're using
the Soviet team, Miyao.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.590
I'm the Hanazono team.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.490
You know, this really makes me happy.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.430
I can't believe you showed off
your scooter to me first.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:10.900
Yes, I didn't think so.
Of course you showed it to Ono first.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.400
So, how did it go?

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.210
Nothing happened.
She was actually kind of cold.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.440
Really?
Something must have happened again.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.180
I bet you'll end up
alienated from each other again.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.050
You never do anything to change that.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.790
I just don't understand the relationship
between you two.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.490
It's irritating watching your feelings
get the better of you.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.230
I don't want to be alienated
from her again.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:45.430
I've kind of known that my feelings
have been getting the better of me.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.700
I've just kept ignoring it.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.940
I don't know what to do.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.170
About what?

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.140
About Ono.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:02.250
Whoa, you finally admitted it
yourself, Haruo!

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.590
What you said, Miyao,

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.750
it was right on target.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:09.620
What was it... I said?

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.530
I've been hiding a lot of things from you
and avoiding your questions.

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.770
To be honest,
I was shocked by my own true feelings.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.000
-You...
-Look at the time.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:23.770
-I've got to get going.
-Wait!

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:27.640
You're so simple-minded,
it's no wonder you didn't know what to do!

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.940
You have no idea what love or romance is!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.580
Love is true! Romance is selfish!

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:36.020
You're not the least bit selfish
after all, Haruo!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.850
<i>For you, there is no "like."</i>

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.090
<i>There's only "love"!</i>

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.990
LIKE
LOVE

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:47.660
You flew past romance, right into love!
It's no wonder you didn't know what to do!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.430
Haruo!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.370
You've finally faced up to
your true feelings!

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.570
Miyao, you're going overboard.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.210
All that about going past romance
into love

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:01.080
doesn't make a whole lot of sense to me.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.250
I'm just a guy who's simply...

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.250
in love...

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.450
with Ono.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.260
<i>Haruo finally spilled his guts.</i>

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:21.000
I see. When you say "spilled his guts,"
you mean he confessed his love.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.370
Was Haruo hiding something?

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.240
Yes, the troubled feelings
that roiled within his heart.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.010
He became aware of them
and came to understand them.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.710
And what is that feeling within his heart?

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.140
Love!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.650
Love!

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:40.620
Love!

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.580
Love?

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.020
LOVE

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:45.950
<i>-Love!
-Love!</i>

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:46.920
Cut it out!

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.090
Who said you could have fun
at my expense in my own room?

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:56.500
Haruo, we're all supporting you,
but at the same time, we're worried.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:59.100
I'm having fun with it, though.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.170
I am too, 30 percent.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.710
Hey! What am I? Your toy?

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:08.680
And who is the other party?
That is the important point.

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.050
Haruo, can I say it?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.880
Sure... I don't care.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.820
It's your younger sister.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.590
Are you... serious?

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.730
I didn't notice at all!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.090
Really? Haruo loves her?

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.030
Is that right?

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:35.300
You have special feelings for
my little sister, Akira?

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.440
Isn't that great, Mrs. Yaguchi?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.540
Yes! I've waited so long!

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:42.510
Yes, it took so long!

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.510
I had always thought that Haruo lacked

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.420
that portion of a boy's adolescence.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:54.720
Haruo must have rushed past romance
and started right in with love.

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.420
Amazing.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:00.730
In elementary school,
I thought Haruo was far beneath me.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.330
Who would have thought he would have
a relationship like that with Ono?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.030
He got into the same high school as me...

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:09.270
works part-time...

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:11.710
and got a scooter license...

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.910
But I get a mere 2,000-yen-a-month
allowance from my mother.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.750
-I'm no match for him!
-Jeez, chill out.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.380
So, what'll you do now?

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.750
Now that you've realized your feelings,
there's no going back.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:28.820
Don't tell me you don't plan on
taking any action at all, do you?

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:34.800
As a man, a male, are you prepared to
carry through with your feelings?

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:38.030
<i>That's right.
Can you carry through with your love?</i>

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:39.900
<i>I did.</i>

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.100
<i>That's why I've got what I have.</i>

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.170
<i>He did too. And him too.</i>

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.080
<i>Haruo, you've grown.</i>

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.110
<i>From II to Champion.</i>

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.150
<i>From Champion to Turbo.</i>

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:55.520
<i>From Turbo to Super!</i>

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.490
<i>Now that you're aware of your growth,</i>

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:02.060
<i>you've evolved to Super Haruo II Turbo!</i>

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.890
<i>That doesn't make any sense!</i>

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.130
<i>Carry through with your love!</i>

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.960
Carry through with your love!

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:09.530
But...

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.270
I don't know how to do that.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.670
Why are you wavering, Haruo?

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.940
This is no time to drag your heels!

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.510
If you tell Ono your true feelings,

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.510
I'm sure she'll be overjoyed.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:26.850
That's right! Invite her on a movie date!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:32.220
Tom's wife, Nicole Kidman's
<i>To Die For</i> is coming out soon!

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:34.290
What movie is that? It sounds cool!

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.220
<i>Jeez, these two sure are a pain.</i>

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.130
Haven't you thought about it at all?

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:41.360
Like what you'll do now.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.470
It's not like
I haven't thought about it at all.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.770
It seems like
Ono is burdened by something too.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:50.300
I know I should do something,

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.970
but I have no idea what it should be.

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:56.880
My own cowardice
irritates the heck out of me.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:00.480
I'm painfully aware of how weak I am.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.050
<i>-It's love!
-It's love!</i>

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.690
<i>-Haruo is truly in love!
-Haruo is truly in love!</i>

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:10.190
What's more,
Ono and I still haven't battled it out.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.790
We haven't settled on who's the best.

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:15.560
I can't feel happy at all right now.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:19.030
Battle? You mean a video game battle?

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:21.500
Are you still thinking about that?

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.870
Yes, that's so like Haruo.
That's who he is.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.540
Rather than a love interest,

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:30.480
Ono is more of a rival to him.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.950
Defeating her first in battle is
core to your beliefs.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:39.820
So, this turns out to be some fight
on some video game or something?

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.120
That's totally outside our expertise.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:44.430
-This is no fun!
-This is no fun!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.230
Since we're not needed here,
let's have tea downstairs.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.100
<i>I guess it makes sense.</i>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:56.970
<i>There's a deep connection
between Haruo and Ono.</i>

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.240
<i>Nobody can come close
to the connection they have,</i>

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:05.450
<i>so urging him to confess his love to her
or propose probably isn't a good idea.</i>

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.750
Then get this game competition over with!

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.650
Quit making a big fuss over it.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:15.320
Say, that competition can be
in <i>Street Fighter II</i>, right?

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:16.920
Yes, I guess so.

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:19.030
Wouldn't this be the way to do it?

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:23.960
The 1996 <i>Super Street Fighter II Turbo</i>
National Championship.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.370
You'll enter this with Ono and win it.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.370
You'll win and confess your love to her.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.970
This way would satisfy you,
wouldn't it, Haruo?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.410
-Where is it held?
-In Osaka.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.580
-Osaka?
-Osaka?

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.080
-The two of them?
-On a trip out of town?

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:46.620
Hey, pomade pussy,
that was a pretty nice suggestion.

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.520
Don't call me a "pomade pussy."

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.560
<i>A competition in Osaka...</i>

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:55.800
<i>Last time, I won because
her buttons were busted.</i>

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.500
<i>That didn't settle anything.</i>

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.970
<i>If she agrees to it,</i>

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.610
<i>I want to settle this in a rematch.</i>

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.950
<i>And if I win...</i>

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.420
"Akira, let's have sex."

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:20.190
Anyway, Haruo,
I know we've pushed you a lot,

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.490
but we are honestly on your side.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:25.960
Right.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.630
"Right." And he had
this totally serious look on his face.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.470
Totally serious, as in "earnest."

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.740
He was earnest!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.070
A trip by Miss Akira out of town?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:40.570
I really doubt
Ms. Moemi would approve of that.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:44.310
What'll you do, Akira?
He's totally serious about this.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.710
He was intent on settling things
once and for all.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.120
I'll admit,

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:52.350
there's definitely a bond between you two
that smacks of fate.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:56.660
What has changed in his heart now?

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:00.630
Why must you settle things
with some final battle now?

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:06.970
Try to understand
Haruo's serious feelings for you, Akira.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.520
<i>The outcome should be determined
before the battle!</i>

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.590
<i>Isn't that what you've always believed?</i>

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:49.210
Super Street Fighter II Turbo<i>.
I've hardly played this at all lately.</i>

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:52.680
<i>I need to get prepped
for when Ono agrees to fight me.</i>

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.720
<i>I'm counting on you, Guile!</i>

00:15:58.850 --> 00:15:59.890
<i>I won't be defeated.</i>

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.860
<i>Not when your love is on the line.</i>

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.410
That chick's amazing!
She has totally freaking mastered this!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.340
She doesn't jump right into the fight!

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.750
She blocks shots with her moves
and closes in! It's frightening!

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.820
You're through if she gets in close!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.350
Using Zangief like that
transforms him from simply Zangief!

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.720
Zangi...

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.220
Zangi-ella!

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.860
Holy shit! She spins the lever
all the way around with such ease!

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.400
It's Zangi-spinner!

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:48.940
-Right! That's so right!
-Right! That's so right!

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:53.270
<i>Haruo was really intent on that</i>
Street Fighter II <i>competition in Osaka.</i>

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:57.480
<i>Try to understand
Haruo's serious feelings for you, Akira.</i>

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:02.780
<i>Besides, taking a trip out of town
with Haruo sounds like a lot of fun.</i>

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.750
<i>I understand
why you can't be honestly happy.</i>

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:12.590
<i>This might be the last time
you spend time together with Haruo.</i>

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:15.560
<i>Also,</i>

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:19.530
<i>you must meet that girl one more time.</i>

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:24.340
HIDAKA SHOP

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:32.580
<i>You're still troubled about
settling things, aren't you?</i>

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:37.720
<i>The boy's heart is on fire
with extraordinary passion for you.</i>

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.120
<i>How will you respond to him?</i>

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:44.890
<i>You should stick close to the path
that you think is best.</i>

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:52.730
HIDAKA SHOP

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:56.640
<i>A trip to Osaka? Outrageous!</i>

00:17:56.700 --> 00:18:00.040
And alone with a man?
I've never heard anything so ridiculous!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:03.180
It's conduct unbecoming of
the daughter of the Ono family.

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:06.280
So, who is this man?

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.320
Is it that Haruo Yaguchi?

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.990
Yes, it is. It's the boy, Yaguchi.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.790
Well, I do appreciate that

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.720
you asked for my permission
without hiding it from me.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.960
However, it's still outrageous!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.870
I'm so dumbfounded by this,
I'll need to return to my home that day.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:31.410
I need to check in on my mother.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:38.710
Isn't that great, Miss Akira?

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:44.180
Ms. Moemi didn't tell you not to go
or say it was unforgivable.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:48.060
In fact, she'll be gone that day
for your sake.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:51.930
This must be how Ms. Moemi shows
her concern for you.

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:34.430
Miss? Miss Makoto?

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.910
Ziiya, has Akira left?

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:42.480
Yes. I took her to Shin-Yokohama Station
around noon.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:45.110
This morning, when I spoke to Mom
on the phone,

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.580
I heard about Akira moving to LA...

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:52.090
and at the end of the month!

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:56.320
It's cruel to force her to live in LA
because it's better for Mom and Dad!

00:19:56.790 --> 00:20:00.290
They'll send her to high school there!
Then to university there!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:05.300
What's worse, they'll force her to marry
the man they've chosen for her!

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:22.480
<i>Did you know, Ziiya?</i>

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:26.650
<i>I heard the decision was made
in early April.</i>

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:27.850
<i>Yes.</i>

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.760
<i>That's about when I heard it.</i>

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.530
I didn't notice at all.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.800
She didn't speak one iota about it.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.570
The end of this month!
Why is this all so sudden?

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.870
Why didn't you tell me?

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:45.140
Are you stupid?

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.270
Well...

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.780
It should have been me.

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:52.280
But since I stopped following orders,

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:55.250
the responsibility
fell onto Akira's shoulders.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.820
Damn the Ono family's desires!

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:01.560
They don't care a single bit
about their daughter's future.

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.290
How can they keep her from
ever returning to Japan?

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.460
Mom and Dad are total morons!

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:10.000
Akira should do as I did
and disobey them too!

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:15.770
Miss Akira wants to do what's best
for her parents and the family.

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:19.670
But still, the end of this month?

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.880
<i>It's way too sudden.</i>

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:27.280
<i>How can I possibly apologize to Akira?</i>

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.290
<i>And Haruo too.</i>

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:42.200
Haruo finally came to grips with
his own feelings.

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:45.430
<i>And Akira practiced like crazy
at the arcade.</i>

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:47.430
<i>She wants to win this.</i>

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:52.670
<i>If she picks up on Haruo's feelings...</i>

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.680
and she's trying to
cut off ties with him...

00:21:58.110 --> 00:21:59.910
<i>If Haruo wins, he'll confess his love.</i>

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.620
<i>If Akira wins, she'll say farewell.</i>

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:41.620
<i>Just riding the Shinkansen to Osaka
gives us a lot of free time.</i>

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:42.950
<i>Okay, Ono...</i>

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:45.620
<i>Wait! What the heck is that
outside the window?</i>

00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:49.420
<i>Hey! Even if it interests you,
don't get off the train!</i>

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:51.460
<i>What'll we do if it leaves without us?</i>

00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:53.030
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
